            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0704" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5041/5a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-22T19:00:00-04:00">January 22, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Department has been informed by Firestone of the provisions of a bill in the
                    Liberian Legislature this week fixing a minimum wage for workmen and “protecting
                    the interest of the working classes.” It is observed that the act is to go into
                    effect on February 1, 1943.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph immediately a report on this measure and an estimation of its
                    effects.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
